u\alpha|x|^{-bp}|u|^{\alpha-2}|v|^{ eta}u\quad	ext{in }\mathbb{R}^n,$$ $$ -\mathrm{div}(|x|^{-2a}
abla v)=|x|^{-bp}|v|^{p-2}v+
u eta|x|^{-bp}|u|^{\alpha}|v|^{ eta-2}v\quad	ext{in }\mathbb{R}^n,$$ $$u,v\in D_a^{1,2}(\mathbb{R}^n),$$ where $n\geq 3,-\infty< a< rac{n-2}{2},a\leq b<a+1,p= rac{2n}{n-2+2(b-a)},
u>0$ and $\alpha>1, eta>1$ satisfying $\alpha+ eta=p$. Our findings are divided into two parts, according to the sign of the parameter $a$. For $a\geq 0$, we demonstrate that any positive solution $(u,v)$ is synchronized, indicating that $u$ and $v$ are constant multiples of positive solutions to the decoupled H'enon equation:  egin{equation*} -\mathrm{div}(|x|^{-2a}
abla w)=|x|^{-bp}|w|^{p-2}w. \end{equation*} For $a<0$ and $b>a$, we characterize all nonnegative ground states. Additionally, we study the nondegeneracy of nonnegative synchronized solutions. This work also delves into some general $k$-coupled H'enon-Sobolev critical systems.

This paper axiomatizes, in a two-stage setup, a new theory for decision under risk and ambiguity. The axiomatized preference relation $\succeq$ on the space $	ilde{V}$ of random variables induces an ambiguity index $c$ on the space $\Delta$ of probabilities, a probability weighting function $\psi$, generating the measure $
u_{\psi}$ by transforming an objective probability measure, and a utility function $\phi$, such that, for all $	ilde{v},	ilde{u}\in	ilde{V}$,  egin{align*} 	ilde{v}\succeq	ilde{u} \Leftrightarrow \min_{Q \in \Delta} \left\{\mathbb{E}_Q\left[\int\phi\left(	ilde{v}^{\centerdot}ight)\,\mathrm{d}
u_{\psi}ight]+c(Q)ight\} \geq \min_{Q \in \Delta} \left\{\mathbb{E}_Q\left[\int\phi\left(	ilde{u}^{\centerdot}ight)\,\mathrm{d}
u_{\psi}ight]+c(Q)ight\}. \end{align*} Our theory extends the rank-dependent utility model of Quiggin (1982) for decision under risk to risk and ambiguity, reduces to the variational preferences model when $\psi$ is the identity, and is dual to variational preferences when $\phi$ is affine in the same way as the theory of Yaari (1987) is dual to expected utility. As a special case, we obtain a preference axiomatization of a decision theory that is a rank-dependent generalization of the popular maxmin expected utility theory. We characterize ambiguity aversion in our theory.

Haglund, Morse, and Zabrocki introduced a family of creation operators of Hall-Littlewood polynomials, $\{C_{a}\}$ for any $a\in \mathbb{Z}$, in their compositional refinement of the shuffle (ex-)conjecture. For any $\alpha\vDash n$, the combinatorial formula for $
abla C_{\alpha}$ is a weighted sum of parking functions. These summations can be converted to a weighted sum of certain LLT polynomials. Thus $
abla C_{\alpha}$ is Schur positive since Grojnowski and Haiman proved that all LLT polynomials are Schur positive. In this paper, we obtain a recursion that implies the $C$-positivity of $(-1)^{k} m_{2^{k}1^{l}}$, and hence prove the Schur positivity of $(-1)^{k}
abla m_{2^{k}1^{l}}$. As a corollary, a parking function interpretation for $(-1)^{k}
abla m_{2^{k}1^{l}}$ is obtained by using the compositional shuffle theorem of Carlsson and Mellit.

